 "about_text": "Ginza Graphic Gallery (ggg) is a gallery devoted to graphic design, established in March 1986 by Dai Nippon Printing Co. in Ginza, Tokyo, an area with a long history of art galleries and close to DNP's founding location. It is planned and operated by the DNP Foundation for Cultural Promotion, with supervision by Kaoru Kasai and Yoshihisa Tanaka. The gallery presents around eight exhibitions a year, inviting designers, artists and organizations from Japan and abroad, or working with collectors, and also runs lectures and publishes gggBooks. Its program focuses on graphic design history and contemporary practice, including posters, book design, and archival material.",
